I just thought that I would get my two cents in on this discussion.
In my opinion the best solution is to implement a confirm on
"dangerous areas"  this should include known traps and pools.  Here is
why I feel this is appropriate.

1.  It really does not detract anything from the game.  It is similar
to an already existing feature namely that of peaceful monsters.

2.  There are times when keyboard input does not match with the
machine processing the input.  Hitting a key not seeing results and
then thinking perhaps the character got lost and hitting it again
causing you to die is not a fun thing.  It has nothing to do with
care.

3.  The arguements against it seem to be of the form: "Well if you are
careful it will never happen".  Theses people have obviously never
dealth with flaky modem connections or slow machines.

4.  It would be relatively simple to code.

5.  It would be relatively simple to put an option in which like for
peaceful monsters would turn of the confirm.

6.  Yes I would be willing to write the code myself if the development
team feels that they don't have the time for it.


